In C#, the `ModelPropertyType` property is not a built-in property. However, you can use the `Type` property to get the type of a property, and then use the `IsPublic` property to check if the property is public.

Here is an example:

```csharp
public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        // Get the type of a property
        Type propertyType = typeof(YourClass).GetProperty("YourProperty").PropertyType;

        // Check if the property is public
        bool isPublic = propertyType.IsPublic;

        Console.WriteLine($"The type of the property is: {propertyType.Name}");
        Console.WriteLine($"Is the property public? {isPublic}");
    }
}
```

In this example, `YourClass` is the name of your class, and `YourProperty` is the name of the property you want to check.

Please replace `YourClass` and `YourProperty` with your actual class
